Sure it can.  I just provide enough extra descriptions so that there are
about 5-6 more descriptions available than there are objects.  When you
get hit by amnesia, I re-randomize any affected object to be either
one of the previously-unused or newly-unused ("forgotten") descriptions.
Won't do you much good to remember that "charging" was VELOX NEB when it
could now be ELBIB YLOH, will it?

Once it gets below about a 20% chance of guessing, the information is
sufficiently "removed" from play that amnesia is simulated effectively.

Is this a good idea?  No; amnesia is already super-annoying for the
player, and something like this just moves mind flayers further up the
geno ladder than they were before.  But let's not get too carried away
with thinking that information is all _that_ fixed.

